  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">All Children Are All Our Children (2019), published by Peter Lang Verlag, has been cited 2 times. Beyond that, it is used in teaching and has 1 formal review.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">All Children Are All Our Children by Doug Selwyn was published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2019. It is part of the Counterpoints series. Conceptually, the work connects to Psychology and Developmental psychology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 2 citations. Citations peaked in 2020 with 1 citing works. Notable citing venues include Educational Psychologist and Postdigital Science and Education. The citing authors are based in the United States. The citation record includes 1 formal book review.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In teaching, it is discussed in 1 recorded lecture. It is recorded in 5 library collections.</p>",
